From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cts: connect a dummy load in the hierarchy as a sink is
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A sink joins its leaf net through hierarchicalConnect; a dummy load,
which CTS adds to balance a leaf net, was connected to the flat net
only. Read back from the .odb, the hierarchical view leaves the dummy
off the net and its capacitance is not seen. On XiangShan's
FltRegionModule, 662 dummy loads. Applies on top of 0111, which joins a
load in the driver's module to the driver's hierarchical net.

Upstream as The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD#11719. Retires on the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that carries
it.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
diff --git a/src/cts/src/TritonCTS.cpp b/src/cts/src/TritonCTS.cpp
--- a/src/cts/src/TritonCTS.cpp
+++ b/src/cts/src/TritonCTS.cpp
@@ -2734,6 +2734,13 @@ void TritonCTS::connectDummyCell(const ClockInst* inst,
   odb::dbNet* sinkNet = iTerm->getNet();
   odb::dbITerm* dummyInputPin = getFirstInput(dummyInst);
   dummyInputPin->connect(sinkNet);
+  // As for a sink: without it the hierarchical view leaves the dummy
+  // load off the net, and its capacitance is gone once the .odb is read
+  // back.
+  if (network_->hasHierarchy()) {
+    network_->hierarchicalConnect(
+        iTerm, dummyInputPin, sinkNet->getConstName());
+  }
   dummyClock.setInputPinObj(dummyInputPin);
   subNet.addInst(dummyClock);
 }
